    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "txt_0469",
      "reading_order": 496,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 339.0803,
        "t": 738.0270068359374,
        "r": 546.5831000000001,
        "b": 727.2077469606776
      },
      "content": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "level": 2,
      "role": "section"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0470",
      "reading_order": 497,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.9375,
        "t": 706.9216068359375,
        "r": 564.8855999999989,
        "b": 608.5099492035389
      },
      "content": "The following procedure serves as a functional voltage regulator check, by determining if the problem is in the voltage regulator or in the generator set. The voltage regulator is temporarily replaced with a 12-volt battery (the generator set starting battery is usable here); 12 volts applied to the F1/F2 exciter stator should produce approximately 125 volts generator set output voltage at L1 and L2, with no load."
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0471",
      "reading_order": 498,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93820000000005,
        "t": 587.2428068359375,
        "r": 565.0073000000007,
        "b": 514.1136519502827
      },
      "content": "WARNING Electrical shock can cause severe personal injury or death.  Do not touch electrical wiring or components during testing.  Disconnect electrical power by removing starting battery negative (-) cable before handling electrical wiring or components.",
      "severity": "warning"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0472",
      "reading_order": 499,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 320.93820000000005,
        "t": 494.04090683593756,
        "r": 564.8983999999994,
        "b": 458.84074920353885
      },
      "content": "Use a sharp voltage probe and touch it carefully to the connector pins or output terminals when making these tests."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0473",
      "reading_order": 500,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2157,
        "t": 443.9249068359376,
        "r": 454.55519999999984,
        "b": 434.0093492035388
      },
      "content": "Stop the generator set."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0474",
      "reading_order": 501,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.2157,
        "t": 424.30970683593756,
        "r": 564.7377999999997,
        "b": 401.7518492035388
      },
      "content": "Unplug the voltage regulator from the wiring harness."
    },
    {
      "type": "admonition",
      "id": "txt_0475",
      "reading_order": 502,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 342.53819999999996,
        "t": 385.7562068359375,
        "r": 564.7975999999999,
        "b": 350.5539519502827
      },
      "content": "CAUTION Failure  to  unplug  the  voltage regulator  at  this  point  in  the  procedure could lead to equipment damage.",
      "severity": "caution"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0476",
      "reading_order": 503,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.215,
        "t": 335.69630683593755,
        "r": 564.7645999999996,
        "b": 300.4389492035388
      },
      "content": "Using jumpers and a spare plug or other connector, connect a 12-volt battery to the F1/F2 terminals as illustrated in Figure 6-6."
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0477",
      "reading_order": 504,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 329.215,
        "t": 290.79540683593757,
        "r": 565.0296999999993,
        "b": 217.61114920353884
      },
      "content": "Start  the  generator  set.    Use  a  voltmeter  to measure the outputs at J4-4 - J4-6, L1 - L2, L1 L0, L2 - L0, Q60 - Q1 (50 Hz sets: Q50 - Q1), and S1 - S2.  The output voltages should read as follows (all voltages apply to both 50 Hz and 60 Hz sets):"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0478",
      "reading_order": 505,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 356.9382,
        "t": 204.04050683593755,
        "r": 557.6626999999999,
        "b": 108.67590683593744
      },
      "content": "J4-4 - J4-6: 62 VAC  20 VAC L1 - L2: 125 VAC  20 VAC L1 - L0: 62 VAC  20 VAC L2 - L0: 62 VAC  20 VAC Q60 - Q1: 75 VAC  20 VAC (50 Hz sets) Q50 - Q1: 75 VAC  20 VAC S1 - S2: 62 VAC  20 VAC"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0479",
      "reading_order": 506,
      "section": "[D] DYNAMIC ROTOR/STATOR TEST",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 342.5386,
        "t": 89.87570683593754,
        "r": 564.7429999999996,
        "b": 54.67554920353871
      },
      "content": "If these voltages are measured, then the generator set is operating correctly and the problem is elsewhere."
    }
  ],
